From: enij90 <226572015+enij90@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: interface: release the wakeup source when the RTC cannot be read

rtc_set_time() and the alarm paths take the RTC parent's wakeup source
with pm_stay_awake() and schedule rtc_timer_do_work(), which releases it
at the end. Since e8ba8a2bc4f6 ("rtc: check if __rtc_read_time was
successful in rtc_timer_do_work()") a failed read returns early without
pm_relax(), so the wakeup source stays active for good.

On the TB321FU rtc0 is rtc-efi and its GetTime fails (EIO). The first
NTP write to rtc0 (RTC_SYSTOHC, chrony rtcsync) leaves "rtc-efi.0"
active, reading /sys/power/wakeup_count then blocks forever, and
Plasma's power button and idle suspend wait 25 s for the powerdevil
helper's D-Bus timeout before suspending.
---
--- a/drivers/rtc/interface.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/interface.c
@@ -980,6 +980,7 @@
 again:
 	err = __rtc_read_time(rtc, &tm);
 	if (err) {
+		pm_relax(rtc->dev.parent);
 		mutex_unlock(&rtc->ops_lock);
 		return;
 	}
